<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tomasi Kulimoetoke II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–2007</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tomasi Kulimoetoke II (1918–2007) was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lavelua">Lavelua</a>, or king, of Uvea (Wallis) in Wallis and Futuna from 1959 until his death. His reign of nearly fifty years spanned the islands' change from French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> to overseas territory in 1961. Its last years were marked by a dispute over his sheltering of a grandson convicted by a French court, which divided the island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tomasi-kulimoetoke-ii.jpg" alt="Tomasi Kulimoetoke II" width="193" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Department of the Interior Office of Insular Affairs official Press Release · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Tomasi_Kulimoetoke.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
